{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in small deterministic specifications. The policy gives clear states a forward-progress bias, routes every obstacle observation through a dedicated recovery state, uses backward motion only for front-obstacle escape, prefers directed turns away from side obstacles, and returns to forward exploration immediately when path_clear is observed. Action states self-loop on path_clear so open-loop pulses are not preempted by non-critical sensing in the same step.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant sensing from actuation so specifications can bind sensor outcomes to exactly one safe controllable action per mode",
    "Use one-shot commit/recovery states: clear -> move_forward, front obstacle -> move_backward, left obstacle -> rotate_clockwise, right obstacle -> rotate_counterclockwise, with fast return to clear on path_clear"
  ],
